<title>NORWAY: SAS HOLDS 1997 FORECAST.</title>
<headline>SAS HOLDS 1997 FORECAST.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scandinavian Airlines System (SAS) said on Wednesday its previous forecast for full-year 1997 earnings to be on a par with 1996 remained unchanged.</p>
<p>&quot;This is based on an anticipated continued positive traffic trend in SAS' markets and a continued moderate increase in unit costs,&quot; SAS said in a statement releasing half-year profits.</p>
<p>&quot;Efforts to achieve structural cost reductions in operations continue and effects of this will appear during the second half and primarily in 1998.&quot;</p>
<p>SAS reported a six percent dip in pre-tax profits up to June 30 at 1.106 billion Swedish crowns, versus 1.178 billion crowns a year ago.</p>
<p>Operating profits before writedowns was 1.936 billion crowns compared with 1.975 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
